WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.651
Telo Ride has to feel quick on a phone, and smooth beside the bike. Now a person can

00:00:07.651 --> 00:00:08.736
measure both.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:16.112
Home loads cold on a mid-range phone's profile: its processor slowed four times,

00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:17.352
over slow 4G.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.135
It must paint within two and a half seconds, and answer every touch within two

00:00:27.135 --> 00:00:28.487
hundred milliseconds.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.334
The race at full HD must hold fifty frames a second, and never drop below thirty for

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:42.810
more than a second.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:51.247
Home, from a phone to the full screen.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:03.180
They run only on the device being measured, when a person asks.

00:01:09.685 --> 00:01:14.288
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:19.145
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.816
every hill and interval.

00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:26.339
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:26.339 --> 00:01:31.787
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:34.777
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:37.615
A custom workout lives under Profile.
